# @scalar/astro@0.4.13 declares `peer astro@"^4.0.0 || ^5.0.0"` and this project
# is on Astro 7, so a strict install refuses to resolve. No published version of
# the integration has widened that range yet — 0.4.13 is latest.
#
# The component itself only uses long-stable Astro API (Astro.props, set:html and
# a bundled <script>), so the range is stale rather than a real incompatibility.
# `npm ci` in the Dockerfile enforces peer ranges too, which is why this lives in
# a file both the image build and local installs read.
#
# Drop this the moment @scalar/astro peers on Astro 7 — it disables peer checking
# for every dependency, so it will hide the next conflict as effectively as it
# hides this one.
legacy-peer-deps=true
